Changelog: 29-10-2026 03:26:16

Release 1.7.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 02:51:30

Added. The header's second line has the power the chip draws and the screen's refresh rate (owner, 29-10-2026:
"power, display Hz"): CPU 47° GPU 45° | 18 W | 120 Hz | 82%, live every five seconds. The power is AMD's driver's
(ADL's ASIC_POWER), left out on a device without it; the refresh rate is the screen the window is on, a TV's when
docked.

Added. A test of the stick lights (owner, 29-10-2026: "I don't see a LED test in the controller test"): the light
icon at the top right of the Controller pane opens it over the window, with Red, Green, Blue, White, Left only,
Right only and Off as pills and what Windows reports about the lamps. It sets them through Windows' Dynamic
Lighting (pywinrt's Windows.Devices.Lights, bundled in the release and listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt), only
while the window is in front; Close gives them back to Armoury Crate. Without lights it says how to switch Dynamic
Lighting on. --lights reads them, writes what Windows reports in the log and exits (a release's check).

