Changelog: 28-10-2026 21:24:56

Release 1.5.0.

Changelog: 28-10-2026 20:49:54

Added. The back buttons M1 and M2 in the controller test, as one M1/M2 chip in the d-pad's row (owner, 28-10-2026: "I
don't see the M1 and M2 buttons"). They never reach Windows as gamepad buttons; the controller reports them on ASUS's
own channel (usage page 0xFF31), read without administrator rights while Armoury Crate runs, and both send the same
code there (tried on the owner's Ally X), so the chip lights for either. A handheld without that channel shows no
M1/M2 chip and counts 15 buttons. The information icon's text says how to map them as two buttons in Armoury Crate.

Changelog: 28-10-2026 20:01:44

Added. The header shows the CPU's and the GPU's temperature, live every five seconds, on a line of its own under
the battery, the date and the time: CPU 47° GPU 45° (owner, 28-10-2026: live in the header, on a second line).
Read without administrator rights and in any Windows language from AMD's driver library (ADL); without it, the GPU's
as Task Manager reads it (D3DKMT) and no CPU temperature.

Fixed. The window fits the Ally's screen again: with the Controller pane it asked for 740 of the 720 px, so the
legend at the bottom was cut off (owner, 28-10-2026). The cards are 100 px high, the controller's chips and sticks a
little closer, and the text about the back buttons M1 and M2 is behind an information icon at the top right
of the Controller pane (owner, 28-10-2026: an icon with a popup where text does not fit, at the top right); it
opens before or after the test.

Changelog: 28-10-2026 19:45:06

Release 1.4.0.

Changelog: 28-10-2026 19:20:52

Added. A Network card (owner, 28-10-2026: the portal's update once came in at 0.8 MB/s where curl had 69 MB/s an
hour later). A on it measures the network in about fifteen seconds: the Wi-Fi link (band, channel, standard, signal
in percent and dBm, the rate down and up), mains or battery with the power plan, the plan's Wi-Fi setting on mains
and on battery, what the handheld received in the two seconds before, Delivery Optimization's downloads and the
programs that download on their own (Steam, the Xbox app and others), and a timed download of the app's newest
release from GitHub, ten seconds at most, kept nowhere. The link and the power setting come from Windows' own APIs
(wlanapi, powrprof), so they read the same in every Windows language; the network's name and the access point's
address are never read out. X saves it in the report as its Network section, after the device's.

Changelog: 28-10-2026 18:12:48

Release 1.3.0.

Changelog: 28-10-2026 18:07:05

Release 1.3.0.

Changelog: 28-10-2026 18:04:37

Added. Two cards beside Device, filled by the same read (owner, 28-10-2026: the Wi-Fi card and any other
hardware; the Device card had room for one more row). Hardware: the built-in panel's size, the touch screen and its
touch points, the Wi-Fi adapter with its driver, the Bluetooth adapter (never a paired device), audio, the fingerprint
reader, a camera, the sensors and the USB controllers. Connected: a dock or a hub (its maker, USB 3 and USB 2: Windows
does not tell a dock from a hub), the external screens and how they are connected, network adapters and drives on
USB; the Device card's Storage lists the built-in drives. X saves one report with a section per card. The read takes
about four seconds.

Added. The header shows the date between the battery and the time: 82% | Wednesday 28/10/2026 | 17:04 (owner,
28-10-2026).

Fixed. A percentage has no space before its sign: 82%, 150% scaling, LT 40% (owner, 28-10-2026).

